  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Tachseer" id="519c-f569-2b89-5182" hidden="false">
      <description>A Legion Command Squad equipped with Legion Scimitar Jetbikes which has Shiban Khan selected as its leader may exchange them for Legion Shamshir Jetbikes at no additional points cost.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Master of the Zadyin Arga" id="8ffb-a95f-9bc8-2608" hidden="false">
      <description>Targutai Yesugei always knows the Telepathy and The Storm&apos;s Fury Psychic Disciplines, and may not select any others. In addition, Targutai Yesugei may take a Dark Sons of Death unit as a Retinue as if he were a Legion Consul with the Stormseer upgrade.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Warlord: Stormseer&apos;s Fury" id="2cc3-6705-b38e-1b81" hidden="false">
      <description>If chosen as the army&apos;s Warlord, Targutai Yesugei automatically has Stormseer&apos;s Fury as his Warlord Trait and may not select any other Warlord Trait.
Targutai Yesugei and any unit he has joined gain the Hatred (Traitors) Special Rule.
In addition, an army with Targutai Yesugei as the warlord gains an additional reaction in the Opposing Player&apos;s Shooting phase as long as Targutai Yesugei has not been removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Warlord: Lord of the Storm" id="e277-2f17-94ca-f9d8" hidden="false">
      <description>If chosen as the army&apos;s Warlord, Shiban Khan automatically has Lord of the Storm as his Warlord Trait and may not select any other Warlord Trait.
In a Detachment with Shiban Khan as your Warlord, any Cavalry unit may re-roll failed Shrouded Damage Mitigation rolls. Shiban Khan and any unit he joins automatically pass Dangerous Terrain tests.
In addition, an army with Shiban Khan as the warlord gains an additional reaction in the Opposing Player&apos;s Assault phase as long as Shiban Khan has not been removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Winds of the Storm" id="f2c9-cbaa-e27b-c5f6" hidden="false">
      <description>A unit that includes any models with this Special Rule may only be joined by a Legion Centurion with the Legiones Consularis: Stormseer upgrade, or by Targutai Yesugei. Legion Techmarines and Legion Apothecaries may not be assigned to a unit with this Special Rule unless they also have this Special Rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Stormseer&apos;s Conclave" id="ac4a-1297-2753-3a74" hidden="false">
      <description>A Wind Rider Squadron in a Detachment that includes a Legion Centurion with the Legiones Consularis: Stormseer upgrade and the Legiones Astartes (White Scars) Special Rule (or Targutai Yesugei) may be selected as a Retinue Squad, instead of as a Fast Attack choice.
A unit selected as a Retinue Squad must be joined by a Stormseer Consul (or Targutai Yesugei), and they must be designated as the unit&apos;s Leader.
A Wind Rider Squadron selected as a Retinue Squad must be deployed with the model selected as its Leader, and the Leader may not voluntarily leave the Retinue Squad during play. A Wind Rider Squadron selected as a Retinue Squad does not use up a Force Organisation slot and is considered part of the same unit as the model selected as its Leader.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
